FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: the-julia-set.
OFF THE RECORD: Compute a Julia set with signed integer arithmetic.
OFF THE RECORD: Coordinates use 10000 units per one. Every pixel starts its
OFF THE RECORD: own orbit z <- z*z + c and stops at escape or 32 iterations.
OFF THE RECORD: No image or orbit is stored in this source.

HEREINAFTER, scale SHALL MEAN 10000.
HEREINAFTER, escape-squared SHALL MEAN 400000000.
HEREINAFTER, iteration-limit SHALL MEAN 32.

ARTICLE 1.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT wide IS 49.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT tall IS 17.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT real-c IS -8000.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT imaginary-c IS 1560.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT ramp IS " .:-=+*#%@".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS "".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS 0.
ARTICLE 2.
    OFF THE RECORD: A terminal cell is about twice as tall as it is wide.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT imaginary-z IS ((tall LESS 1) LESS 2 TIMES row) TIMES 32000 APPORTIONED AMONG (wide LESS 1).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS 0.
ARTICLE 3.
    OFF THE RECORD: A symmetric grid includes both axes and all four corners.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT real-z IS (2 TIMES column LESS (wide LESS 1)) TIMES 16000 APPORTIONED AMONG (wide LESS 1).
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT age IS THE FINDING OF escape-age REGARDING real-z AND imaginary-z AND real-c AND imaginary-c.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS THE FINDING OF escape-shade REGARDING age.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT column IS column PLUS 1.
    SHOULD column FALL SHORT OF wide, REFER TO ARTICLE 3.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT frame IS frame PLUS "\n".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT row IS row PLUS 1.
    SHOULD row FALL SHORT OF tall, REFER TO ARTICLE 2.
    PROCLAIM frame.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.

THE OFFICE OF escape-age, CONCERNING zx AND zy AND cx AND cy.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT orbit-age IS 0.
SECTION 1.
    OFF THE RECORD: Test the old orbit before computing the next one. The
    OFF THE RECORD: old real and imaginary values must serve both products.
    SHOULD zx TIMES zx PLUS zy TIMES zy EXCEED escape-squared, REMAND WITH orbit-age.
    SHOULD orbit-age EQUAL iteration-limit, REMAND WITH orbit-age.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT next-real IS (zx TIMES zx LESS zy TIMES zy) APPORTIONED AMONG scale PLUS cx.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT zy IS 2 TIMES zx TIMES zy APPORTIONED AMONG scale PLUS cy.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT zx IS next-real.
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT orbit-age IS orbit-age PLUS 1.
    REFER TO SECTION 1.

THE OFFICE OF escape-shade, CONCERNING age.
    OFF THE RECORD: At the limit, a pixel is unresolved, not proved interior.
    SHOULD age EQUAL iteration-limit, REMAND WITH "@".
    LET IT BE RECORDED THAT shade-index IS 1 PLUS age TIMES 9 APPORTIONED AMONG iteration-limit.
    REMAND WITH AN EXCERPT OF ramp FROM shade-index TO shade-index.
